{
  "dom_id": "step-q213335",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $9,$ the additive inverse of $27$ modulo $9$ is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $27$ modulo $9$ is the integer $0\\le x<9$ such that\n\n$$\nx+27≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9).\n$$\n\nFirst, note that $27≡3\\cdot 9≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ and $0+0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9).$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $27$ modulo $9$ is $0.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n27+0≡3\\cdot 9+0≡3\\cdot 0+0≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
